-/-!
-### Invariance under an embedding
-
-The absolute height is attached to the algebraic numbers themselves: an embedding of fields of
-characteristic zero leaves it unchanged. This is what makes a value computed over `ℚ` readable
-inside `ℝ` or `ℂ`, where `absMulHeight_eq` does not apply because the ambient field is not a
-number field.
--/
